  "raw": "en Español\n\n824 \nABNT20 KNHC 291133\nTWOAT \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n800 AM EDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nFor the North Atlantic...Caribbean Sea and the Gulf of America:\n\nEast of the Leeward Islands (Remnants of Dolly):\nShowers and thunderstorms have increased this morning in \nassociation with the remnants of Tropical Storm Dolly, located \nseveral hundred miles east of the Leeward Islands. However, there \nare no signs that the system is developing a closed circulation.\nRedevelopment of this system is unlikely while it moves westward to \nwest-northwestward near 25 mph.  The wave could bring locally heavy \nrains and gusty winds to portions of the Leeward Islands, the Virgin \nIslands and Puerto Rico over the next several days.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...10 percent.\n\nNortheastern and North-Central Gulf of America:\nDisorganized cloudiness and showers over portions of the \nnortheastern and north-central Gulf of America are associated with a \nweak area of low pressure centered about 100 miles south-southwest \nof Pensacola, Florida.  Development, if any, of this system is \nexpected to be slow while it drifts westward for the next few days.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...10 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Beven"
